{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Use to see what one session (id from list_sessions) would have cost on another model: the session's own request trace (token counts only) is run through that model's vendor caching rules and priced, turn by turn beside what the session really cost. Every figure is Simulated, not measured: it assumes the same conversation (A1: the other model gets the same prompts and answers with as many tokens, which it wouldn't) and the same token counts (A2); the answer lists every assumption. Say \"would have cost about\", never \"would have cost\". The self-check (selfCheck) is the same replay on the session's own model compared with its log (cache read within 5%): if it didn't pass, trust the figures less; null when the own model has no vendor profile; models lists every model it ran when the session switched. Totals compare like with like (the turns replayed with a known measured and simulated cost); coverage gives the turns and requests not replayed with their reasons (helperRequests: Copilot helper agents' requests such as the todo list and the conversation summary, left out because each has a prompt of its own; their cost stays in the measured figures; subagentRuns: the subagent runs a Copilot Chat or Claude Code session's replay leaves out, because it covers the main agent only, with their tokens and cost; Claude Code runs started off the active branch are not counted.), and an unknown figure is null with a reason, never 0. A session whose provider's logs can't be replayed yet answers with the reason.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"model":{"description":"A model id a vendor profile lists, e.g. \"claude-haiku-5.5\" or \"gpt-6.1-sol\" (log spellings such as \"claude-opus-5-5-202